# Environment variables for Waxhaw Connect.
# Copy to .env.local for development and add the same values to the Vercel
# project as Environment Variables.
#
# Two kinds of value live here, and the prefix is what separates them. Vite
# inlines every VITE_ prefixed variable into the browser bundle, so those are
# public by definition. Unprefixed variables stay on the server and are read
# only by the handlers under api/. Never add a VITE_ prefix to one of those.

# Firebase web config. These are browser keys. Firebase publishes them in
# client bundles by design, so they are not secrets. Access is controlled by
# firestore.rules, not by hiding these values.
#
# Find them in the Firebase console:
# Project settings > General > Your apps > SDK setup and configuration.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Gemini API key, server-side only. Used by api/assist.js for the
# plain-language resource matcher and the event paste parser.
# Create one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey

GEMINI_API_KEY=
